# Copy this file to .env (git-ignored) for local builds, or set the same
# names as repository *variables* (not secrets - they end up in the public
# client bundle either way) under GitHub → Settings → Secrets and variables
# → Actions → Variables, so .github/workflows/static.yml can pass them into
# `npm run build`. See README's "AI Schedule-Photo Import" section
# for what each one is for and how to set up the service behind it.

# Base URL of the deployed Cloudflare Worker (source lives in the separate
# JayPengX/shared-proxy repo, see its README for setup), e.g.
# https://orbit-ai-gemini-proxy.<you>.workers.dev - no path suffix. This one
# Worker backs the app's AI features: schedule-photo import (/gemini) and
# natural-language schedule edits (/nl-edit, src/editor-nl-edit.js) - each
# module appends its own hardcoded path (see src/proxy-config.js), so there
# is one URL to set instead of one per feature. (Sync is the Quadra Pass's,
# through the shared kit, src/sync.js.) There is no bring-your-own-key
# fallback - a fork built from source with no proxy deployed yet just
# leaves both AI features unavailable.
VITE_PROXY_URL=
